From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mbt28 <btekbas@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: suniv: take the DRAM clock from CONFIG_DRAM_CLK

dram_suniv.c hardcodes 156 MHz and ignores CONFIG_DRAM_CLK, which the
suniv board defconfigs set (to the same 156), so the clock cannot be
changed from the configuration. Use the option, as the other DRAM
drivers do. The PLL_DDR steps make it a multiple of 12 MHz here; the
fixed cycle timings of this driver (tRFC 13 cycles >= 70 ns) hold up to
180 MHz.

No change at the default.

Signed-off-by: mbt28 <btekbas@gmail.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_suniv.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_suniv.c
@@ -55,7 +55,7 @@
 
 struct dram_para suniv_dram_para = {
 	.size = 32,
-	.clk = 156,
+	.clk = CONFIG_DRAM_CLK,
 	.access_mode = 1,
 	.cs_num = 1,
 	.ddr8_remap = 0,
